text:
maria: quick check — seeing malformed JSON errors in our node streaming client when server sends large messages; looks like chunk boundaries split an object mid-utf8 and the parser dies. anyone seen this? attaching minimal repro.

kevin: yep — if you rely on Buffer.toString() per chunk you'll split UTF-8 codepoints. use a streaming TextDecoder or keep an unfinished tail. also common to see backpressure: consumer slower than arriving chunks -> internal queue grows.

elyse: repro?

maria: pasted snippet:
```
// naive
stream.on('data', (b) => {
  const s = b.toString('utf8')
  const obj = JSON.parse(s)
  handle(obj)
})
```
This fails when s is partial.

kevin: instead do:
```
const td = new TextDecoder('utf-8')
let buf = new Uint8Array(0)
stream.on('data', (chunk) => {
  buf = concat(buf, new Uint8Array(chunk))
  const decoded = td.decode(buf, {stream:true})
  // push into incremental JSON parser (clarinet/sax-like)
})
```
Or use ndjson separators if you can change server.

maria: server is hosted API can't change easily. can we drop a fix in node SDK to handle partial JSON + bounded queue? proposal: 1) TextDecoder streaming, 2) incremental parser fallback, 3) cap queue length and apply backpressure via pausing the underlying stream and emit warning.

jia: +1. For python SDK, similar: use codecs.getincrementaldecoder('utf-8') and ijson for incremental JSON.

elyse: ping @eng-runtime — would pausing the socket be safe w/ our server's connection model? might affect keepalive.

dev-bot: deploy reminder: eng-runtime oncall rotation today is @sam.

kevin: pausing is ok for short windows; ensure you set a max buffer size and timeouts to avoid dead consumers. Also add metrics: queue_depth, avg_chunk_delay, parse_errors.

maria: I'll open PR with tests (node+python) + a small e2e that simulates split codepoints and big objects. assign reviewers kevin/elyse. any ptr on where to put tests?

elyse: tests under devex/streaming-integration and add a flaky guard for CI.

maria: thanks! I'll also add a small note in docs about ndjson preference and server-side heuristics. :thumbsup:
